Phase 1 micro-checkpoint 2 — server-only, read-only.

Adds GET /providers/application/status: a compact, owner-scoped view that
turns the current application state into a single response the eventual
web and mobile rejected-state screens can rely on. The endpoint gives the
provider exactly what they need to see next — the current status, the
reviewer's rejection reason if any, a submission history summary, and a
server-derived nextAction plus canEdit/canReset/canResubmit flags — so
the UI never has to guess or duplicate rules.

- Reuses getOwnApplication so reviewer-private reviewerNotes cannot leak
  into responses; the test file verifies both the field name and the
  private phrase itself are absent.
- Owner-only via requireAuth + assertProviderMember; client tokens 403,
  unauthenticated 401.
- Server-derived nextAction covers all five status values (draft,
  under_review, approved, rejected, suspended).
- Approved-provider authorization and careNotes privacy remain unchanged.
- Focused test:provider-status covers draft, under_review, rejected,
  reset+history, multi-cycle counts, approved (with provider ops
  regression), and suspended (with provider ops still blocked).
- Regressions green locally: provider-resubmission 11/11, authorization
  7/7, care-history 4/4, role-state 2/2, reviews 7/7, availability 3/3,
  booking state-machine 63/63, booking-concurrency 16/16, booking-pressure
  13/13, full workspace typecheck + build.
